# Resume Value

Instead of saying:

> Built a React CRUD app.

You can say:

> Designed and developed a cloud-native Construction Operations Platform using a microservice architecture. Implemented Kubernetes deployments, Infrastructure as Code with Terraform, CI/CD pipelines, event-driven workflows, secure document management, and AI-powered document search using RAG and LLMs.

That is a much stronger story.

## I would build it in this order

1. **Project & Organization Management** (organizations, projects, users, roles)
2. **Workforce & Site Operations** (attendance, site diary, tasks, safety)
3. **Materials & Equipment** (inventory, rentals, maintenance)
4. **Documents & Approvals** (drawings, RFIs, contracts, versioning)
5. **Procurement & Finance** (purchase orders, invoices, budgets)
6. **AI Layer** (RAG search, summaries, document assistant)
7. **Cloud & Production** (Kubernetes, Terraform, monitoring, CI/CD, autoscaling)

This progression lets you continuously add technical depth while always having a working product, and every phase introduces opportunities to showcase modern software engineering practices.
